course: dictionary
lesson: 6078
title: Words with a big meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words carry a lot of meaning. Context helps you see which meaning fits. In «Jews do not accept Jesus as the Messiah; Muslims honour him as a great prophet but not as God's Son», the Messiah is a religious title, and people of different faiths see it in different ways.
explain: A capital M means one special figure in religion. «Handel's Messiah» is a famous piece of music, sung at Christmas and Easter. A small m, as in «a messiah», means any leader that people hope will save them or solve their problems.
explain: Read the feeling in the sentence. A messiah is sometimes said with doubt, which means people may be hoping too much. To check a meaning, swap it into the sentence and ask if it still makes sense.
fact: «Messiah» comes from a Hebrew word meaning «anointed one».
fact: «Christ» is the Greek word for the same idea.
fact: Jewish people are still waiting for the Messiah, while Christians believe the Messiah came in Jesus.
fact: A capital M means the special religious figure; a small m, «a messiah», means any leader people hope will save them.
fact: «The promised Messiah» means the Messiah people were promised would come.
exercise: «Jews do not accept Jesus as the Messiah; Muslims honour him as a great prophet but not as God's Son.» What does this tell you about the Messiah? | *A religious figure that people of different faiths see in different ways | It is a bread that is baked at Easter | It is a town on the coast | It is a team that plays in the summer
exercise: Ella says, «Handel's Messiah is on the radio every Christmas.» What kind of thing is Handel's Messiah? | *A famous piece of music, often sung at Christmas | A kind of football team | A new type of phone | A school subject
exercise: Mia says, «My uncle is a messiah for our football team.» What does a messiah mean here? | A kind of kit with stripes | A player who never scores | *A leader people hope will save them or solve their problems | A referee who blows the whistle
test: «Christians believe that Jesus is the Messiah.» What does this sentence tell you? | Christians think the Messiah is a bird | Christians never go to church | Christians think Jesus is a special figure in their religion | *Christians think Jesus lived in a castle
test: Which word in the sentence «Muslims honour him as a great prophet» tells you the Muslims respect him? | him | honour | great | *prophet
exam: What is the difference between «the Messiah» with a capital M and «a messiah» with a small m? | *The capital M means a special religious figure, and the small m means any leader people hope will save them | The capital M means a special religious figure, while the small m means any leader people hope will save them | The capital M means a cake and the small m means a sweet | They mean exactly the same, so the capital letter does not matter
